                <pb facs="0950" n="814" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg814"/>

                <head>No. 590.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Herbert to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>. <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 1, 1888</date>.
                        (Received August 2.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: At the desire of Her Majesty’s principal
                    secretary of state for foreign affairs, I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    copy of Mr. Justice Prowse’s report on certain alleged breaches, of the
                    Newfoundland bait act by American fisherman.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arthur Herbert</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>(In the absence of Sir Lionel West.)</p>
                </postscript>

















